  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Gufran Buffalo Meat Shop Thru. ... vs State Of U.P. Thru. Secy. Deptt. Of Food ... on 6 February, 2024 Author: Vivek Chaudhary Bench: Vivek Chaudhary High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ? Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:10807-Db Court No. - 2 Case :- Writ - C No. - 1160 of 2024 Petitioner :- M/S Gufran Buffalo Meat Shop Thru. Proprietor Mohd. Gufran Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Secy. Deptt. Of Food Safety And Drug Administration U. Counsel for Petitioner :- Vinay Prakash Shukla,Arun Kumar Yadav Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C.,Hemendra Kumar Bhatt Hon'ble Vivek Chaudhary,J. Hon'ble Om Prakash Shukla,J. Heard learned counsel for the petitioner, learned Standing Counsel for the State/respondents and Sri Hemendra Kumar Bhatt, learned counsel appearing for the Nagar Palika Parishad, Mahmudabad, District Sitapur. Petitioner has approached this Court for a mandamus claiming that he having a license from the Department of Food Safety and Drug Administration, Government of U.P. and the Nagar Palika Parishad should not interfere in his business. M/S Gufran Buffalo Meat Shop Thru. ... vs State Of U.P. Thru. Secy. Deptt. Of Food ... on 6 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/187345947/ 1 Learned counsel for the Nagar Palika Parishad states that there is a notice already given to the petitioner but it appears that a fresh notice is required to be given to the petitioner.",
